        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-grammar-fill-title",
              "text": "Xiao long bao (soup dumplings) , those amazing constructions of delicate dumpling wrappers, encasing hot,  __56__ (taste) soup and sweet, fresh meat, are far and away my favorite Chinese street food. The dumplings arrive steaming and dangerously hot. To eat one, you have to decide whether  __57__ (bite) a small hole in it first, releasing the stream and risking a spill (溢出) ,  __58__to put the whole dumpling in your mouth, letting the hot soup explode on your tongue. Shanghai may be the  __59__ (recognize) home of the soup dumplings but food historians will actually point you to the neighboring canal town of Nanxiang as Xiao long Bao’s birthplace. There you will find them prepared differently – more dumpling and less soup, and the wrappers are pressed  __60__hand rather than rolled. Nanxiang aside, the best Xiao long bao have a fine skin, allowing them  __61__ (lift) out of the steamer basket without allowing them tearing or spilling any of  __62__ (they) contents. The meat should be fresh with __63__touch of sweetness and the soup hot, clear and delicious. No matter where I buy them, one steamer is  __64__ (rare) enough, yet two seems greedy, so I am always left  __65__ (want) more next time."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "group-2023-i-writing-application": {
        "groupId": "group-2023-i-writing-application",
        "groupType": "writing",
        "title": "应用文写作",
        "questionIds": [],
        "writingTaskId": "wt-2023-i-application",
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-title",
              "text": "假定你是李华，外教Ryan准备将学生随机分为两人一组，让大家课后练习口语，你认为这样分组存在问题。请你给外教写一封邮件，内容包括："
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p1",
              "text": "1. 说明问题；"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p2",
              "text": "2. 提出建议。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p3",
              "text": "1. 写作词数应为80个左右；"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p4",
              "text": "2. 请按如下格式在答题卡的相应位置作答。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p5",
              "text": "Dear Ryan,"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p6",
              "text": "I’m Li Hua from Class 3."
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p7",
              "text": "Yours sincerely,"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-app-p8",
              "text": "Li Hua"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "group-2023-i-writing-continuation": {
        "groupId": "group-2023-i-writing-continuation",
        "groupType": "writing",
        "title": "读后续写",
        "questionIds": [],
        "writingTaskId": "wt-2023-i-continuation",
        "passage": {
          "paragraphs": [
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-title",
              "text": "阅读下面材料, 根据其内容和所给段落开头语续写两段, 使之构成一篇完整的短文。"
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-p1",
              "text": "When I was in middle school, my social studies teacher asked me to enter a writing contest. I said no without thinking. I did not love writing. My family came from Brazil, so English was only my second language. Writing was so difficult and painful for me that my teacher had allowed me to present my paper on the sinking of the Titanic by acting out a play, where I played all the parts. No one laughed harder than he did."
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-p2",
              "text": "So, why did he suddenly force me to do something at which I was sure to fail? His reply: “Because I love your stories. If you’re willing to apply yourself, I think you have a good shot at this.” Encouraged by his words, I agreed to give it a try."
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-p3",
              "text": "I chose Paul Revere’s horse as my subject. Paul Revere was a silversmith (银匠) in Boston who rode a horse at night on April 18, 1775 to Lexington to warn people that British soldiers were coming. My story would come straight from the horse’s mouth. Not a brilliant idea, but funny; and unlikely to be anyone else’s choice."
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-p4",
              "text": "What did the horse think, as he sped through the night? Did he get tired? Have doubts? Did he want to quit? I sympathized immediately. I got tired. I had doubts. I wanted to quit. But, like Revere’s horse, I kept going. I worked hard. I checked my spelling. I asked my older sister to correct my grammar. I checked out a half dozen books on Paul Revere from the library. I even read a few of them."
            },
            {
              "paragraphId": "para-2023-i-writing-cont-p5",
              "text": "When I handed in the essay to my teacher, he read it, laughed out loud, and said, “Great. Now, write it again.” I wrote it again, and again and again. When I finally finished it, the thought of winning had given way to the enjoyment of writing. If I didn’t win, I wouldn’t care."
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
